    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0413" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">625.5131/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-04T18:00:00-04:00">February 4, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. Department’s 5, February 1, 2 p.m. In the absence of the Minister,<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d287-f1"/> the Undersecretary for Foreign Affairs<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d287-f2"/> informs me that <pb facs="0414" n="315"
                        xml:id="pg315"/> the new French-Chilean Commercial Convention has been put
                    into force provisionally but that the French-Chilean <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >modus vivendi</hi> of May 22, 1931 will not be denounced until the date of
                    ratification of the new agreement. He added that in any event our <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> of September 28, 1931 will remain in
                    force until the date of formal ratification.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
